1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,883
An EC2 server has a high severity vulnerability. The
security workflow captures the alert.

2
00:00:06,883 --> 00:00:13,117
This is a simulated example, using fictional findings
and no live AWS data.

3
00:00:13,117 --> 00:00:20,184
An AI assistant checks the finding and explains the
security risk in plain language.

4
00:00:20,184 --> 00:00:26,116
It prepares a proposed patch and makes the reasoning
visible for review.

5
00:00:26,116 --> 00:00:33,251
Before anything changes, a person reviews the plan and
approves the proposed action once.

6
00:00:33,251 --> 00:00:39,116
The human approval gate keeps production changes from
running automatically.

7
00:00:39,116 --> 00:00:45,732
After approval, AWS Systems Manager would apply the
patch to the affected server.

8
00:00:45,732 --> 00:00:52,117
This video is a simulation. No command runs and nothing
is changed in AWS.

9
00:00:52,117 --> 00:00:58,406
Finally, the workflow would verify the result and
record evidence for the audit trail.

10
00:00:58,406 --> 00:01:05,117
Detection, human approval, action, and verification
stay connected and visible.
